@startuml

!include ../../../../../../tooling/styles/plantuml/structural/package-diagram-style.iuml

title Breaking a Uses Cycle via Dependency Inversion

package "BEFORE: Cyclic Dependency" as BEFORE $deep_invalid {
  rectangle "User Interface\n(Module A)" as A1 $fill_invalid
  rectangle "Business Logic\n(Module B)" as B1 $fill_invalid

  A1 -right-> B1 : <<uses>>\noperations
  B1 -left-> A1 : <<uses>>\nnotifications
}

note bottom of BEFORE
  **Problem:** Neither A nor B
  can be developed, tested,
  or deployed independently
end note

package "AFTER: Cycle Broken" as AFTER $deep_ok {
  rectangle "User Interface\n(Module A)" as A2 $fill_ok
  rectangle "<<interface>>\nNotificationListener" as IF $fill_caution
  rectangle "Business Logic\n(Module B)" as B2 $fill_ok

  A2 -right-> B2 : <<uses>>\noperations
  B2 -down-> IF : <<uses>>\nnotifies via interface
  A2 .down.> IF : <<implements>>
}

note bottom of AFTER
  **Solution:** B defines an interface;
  A implements it. B depends on
  the interface, not on A directly.
  No cycle remains.
end note
@enduml
